The rendered site is what a reader actually judges, and several of these are
invisible from inside the repo.

`gjli` is the standing rule (all UI follows accessibility guidelines) and
`rptk` is a live instance of breaking it. `blv9` and `g4dv` are links that do
not resolve or do not land where they claim; `1le7` and `alox` are surfaces
that shipped with their judgement calls unrecorded.

Grouped because they share a verification problem rather than a subject: none of
them can be confirmed by a passing test suite, and all of them need somebody to
LOOK at a deployed page.
